  "body": "## Change and scope\n\nAt base `0b1cccf86e2f5132ed286a26ef0a681a495740ea`, the historical mixed-point audit (`scripts/audit_mixed_point.py`) and the early-sharing screen both call `scalar_check` on large cancellation-free circuits. Profiling shows a large share of that helper\u2019s time in per-node `json.dumps((node, args), \u2026)` and per-output `json.dumps((i, node), \u2026)` while building `circuit_sha256`.\n\nThis PR writes the same UTF-8 digest lines with an equivalent hand-rolled formatter (`[node,null]`, `[node,[a,b]]`, `[i,node]`), keeps every support and topology `require`, and leaves `circuit_sha256` unchanged. No certificate `source_sha256` pin lists `audit_mixed_point.py`; the mixed-point and early-sharing mathematical payloads stay fieldwise identical to the committed files.\n\n**Tooling improvement; no new kappa.** Selected frontier untouched.\n\n## Result\n\nOn Linux / CPython 3.12.3 (Linux-6.12.94+-x86_64-with-glibc2.39), five alternating fresh-process pairs timing only `scalar_check` on the fixed mixed-point circuit set gave median wall time **10.004 \u2192 4.444 seconds (2.25\u00d7)**. Timing is host-descriptive and is not a correctness gate. Every scalar receipt matches the baseline checker fieldwise (`roles`, `circuit_sha256`, flags).\n\nPackage: `research/mixed-point-scalar-digest/`.\n\n## Validation\n\n```sh\npython3.12 -I -B research/mixed-point-scalar-digest/verify.py\npython3.12 -I -O -B research/mixed-point-scalar-digest/verify.py\npython3.12 -B scripts/research_package.py --package research/mixed-point-scalar-digest\npython3.12 -I -B research/mixed-point-scalar-digest/benchmark.py --rounds 5\n```\n\nExpected:\n\n```text\nPASS_MIXED_POINT_SCALAR_DIGEST scalar_cases=7 encoding_cases=5 certs=0 no_new_kappa\nPASS_REGISTERED_RESEARCH_PACKAGE research/mixed-point-scalar-digest outcome=completed\nPASS_IDENTICAL_MIXED_POINT_SCALAR_RECEIPTS\n```\n\nDefault verify is read-only. Full `make verify`, selected cold replay, Lean, and multiplication-theorem obligations were not rerun for this isolated historical-checker change.\n\n## Overlap and credit\n\nClosest priors (different objects): [CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds#756](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/756), [CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds#1793](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1793), [CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds#1861](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1861), [CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds#1922](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1922), [CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds#1217](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1217), and `research/rational-containment-performance/` (mixed-point `contained` adapter). Open [CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds#1874](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1874) optimizes a different hosted-audit digest path and does not touch `scalar_check`. No competing open PR on the `scalar_check` digest object at refresh.\n\nDouglas R. Colkitt authored the mixed-point and early-sharing screens and original checkers. Prepared by Wentao Li ([VictorLiwentao](https://github.com/VictorLiwentao), [@Is__Victor](https://x.com/Is__Victor)) with substantial AI assistance, under Apache-2.0.",
